.TH smi-incoming-deploy "1" "September 2026" "SMI Toolset" "SMI Base Command"
.SH NAME
smi-incoming-deploy \- Hand incoming deployment packages to deployment plugins
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smi-incoming-deploy
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
.B smi-incoming-deploy
processes deployment packages dropped into the incoming directory: for every
.B .tar.gz
file in
.I /var/opt/setmy.info/incoming
it runs each executable
.B .sh
plugin from
.I /opt/setmy.info/lib/incoming
with the package path as the only argument.
What a package means is entirely up to the plugins.
.PP
The command is quiet by design: a missing incoming directory, an empty one, or an absent
plugin directory all end with success, so it is safe to run from cron or a timer.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/opt/setmy.info/incoming
Incoming packages, one
.B .tar.gz
per deployment.
.TP
.I /opt/setmy.info/lib/incoming
Deployment plugins, executable
.B .sh
files.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Every plugin ran successfully, or there was nothing to do.
.SH AUTHOR
Imre Tabur <imre.tabur@mail.ee>
